  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA weak cold front is currently moving across the region early\nthis morning. Patchy low-level clouds and fog are expected to\ndevelop, with high-resolution models continuing to highlight \nthe area of I-70 as the greatest potential for dense fog between\n5am and 9am. Visibility is expected to improve after 9am with\nsurface heating. \n\nOverall, quiet and dry conditions with above-average\ntemperatures will remain the primary forecast story over the\nnext several days as high pressure dominates. A passing cold\nfront early Friday morning will increase low-level clouds,\nthrough precipitation chances remain low. \n\nThe best potential for widespread rainfall continues to be\nSunday afternoon into Monday morning as a large-scale\ndisturbance develops over the southern Plains and tracks\neastward. The probability of impactful rainfall remains low,\nbelow 30%. However, with significant leaf accumulation on the\nground, clogged storm drains could contribute to areas of\nstanding water on Monday.",
